# This project is authored on Windows and runs on Linux, and Git on Windows is
# configured with core.autocrlf=true — so without this every file would be
# checked out with CRLF endings.
#
# For a shell script that is not cosmetic: the kernel reads `#!/bin/bash\r`
# as an interpreter named "bash\r", which does not exist, and the only
# symptom is a script that refuses to run for no visible reason. The systemd
# unit fails the same way.
#
# The Dockerfile already strips CR defensively at build time. This is the fix
# one level up, so the files are correct before they ever get there.
* text=auto eol=lf
